WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.940
Hello, I'm Tealy.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.420
I love reading.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.720
And here's my secret for main idea questions:

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.860
it's all about size.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.120
A main idea has to be the right size.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.800
It covers the central point of the passage.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.060
Not just one small detail.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.620
And not some giant claim the passage never made.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.220
Here's a passage.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.900
A neighborhood garden planted native flowers.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:29.480
Over two summers,

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.720
those flowers drew more visits from local pollinators.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.360
Too narrow: the garden planted flowers.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.480
True, but just a detail.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:42.380
Too broad: all gardens everywhere save pollinators.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.220
The passage never said that.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:48.580
Just right: this neighborhood garden increased local pollinator

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:49.480
visits.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:51.740
Here's the fast way.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.580
Before you look at the options,

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.880
write a short headline for the passage.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.340
Like a newspaper.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.700
Garden draws more local pollinators.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.740
Then find the answer that matches.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.220
Your turn. A town's new bike lane cut commute times for

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.040
local riders. Main idea?

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.380
Choice A: bikes are the best way to travel.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.820
Choice B: one town's bike lane helped its riders.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:17.380
Go.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.620
B! Choice A goes way bigger than the passage.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.760
Watch for words like always,

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:31.700
and all. They need very strong support.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:33.580
If the author said some,

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.520
or may, your answer can't say always.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:39.460
Match the author's scope,

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.260
and how certain they are.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:42.940
Now hit Try this skill,

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:43.960
and happy reading!
